==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|lang=goh|wizzan}}, originally *{{term||wittan}}. Cognates include Swedish {{term|veta}} and archaic Modern English verb {{term|wit#Verb|wit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|DE-wissen.ogg|audio}}
* {{audio|BY-wissen.ogg|Audio (Bavarian)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|weiß|wusste|gewusst}}

# {{transitive|or|intransitive}} To [[know]]; to be [[aware]] of (a fact).
#: ''Ich '''weiß''', wo du bist.'' — “I know where you are.”
#: ''von etwas '''wissen''''' — “to know about something”

